1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:01,500
<i> Here's what I found out.</i>

2
00:00:01,633 --> 00:00:03,567
<i>The receptionist is her cousin.</i>

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,467
<i>Did she give it to you?
Golda's number?</i>

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,567
<i> No.</i>

5
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,333
<i>You've been staring at me
since I sat down.</i>

6
00:00:08,467 --> 00:00:10,367
<i>- Who are you?
- That's a former cop, Boss!</i>

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,133
<i>A terror during drug busts
but turns out he's a cop killer.</i>

8
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:15,900
<i>Ramon Orbos, the cop
they say I killed...</i>

9
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:17,200
<i> do you know him?</i>

10
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:19,133
<i>You know what my mother
always used to say?</i>

11
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:21,833
<i> Don't talk to strangers.</i>

12
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:22,833
<i> There she is.</i>

13
00:00:22,967 --> 00:00:23,933
<i> Let's go.</i>

14
00:00:24,067 --> 00:00:25,067
<i> Wait, the bag's gone.</i>

15
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,067
<i> She left it inside.</i>

16
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,433
<i>Golda is coming from there,
right?</i>

17
00:00:27,567 --> 00:00:28,867
<i>- But when?
- We don't know yet,</i>

18
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,100
<i> but she will show up.</i>

19
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:31,100
<i> She's here.</i>

20
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:32,933
<i> If my instinct is correct,</i>

21
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:34,133
<i> that bag contains the money,</i>

22
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:35,733
<i> and Golda will come to get it.</i>

23
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:36,967
<i> That is how she collects.</i>

24
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:38,133
<i> How did you find me?</i>

25
00:00:38,267 --> 00:00:39,800
<i> No one knows you're here.</i>

26
00:00:39,933 --> 00:00:41,367
<i> I'm Miguel Delgado's daughter.</i>

27
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,433
<i>Golda, please,
have mercy on my father!</i>

28
00:00:43,567 --> 00:00:45,733
<i>You know what happened
to Parak, right?</i>

29
00:00:45,867 --> 00:00:47,833
<i>I don't want to end up like him!</i>

30
00:00:47,967 --> 00:00:48,700
<i> Don't come near me!</i>

31
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:49,967
<i> Stop following me!</i>

32
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:52,733
<i> She can't escape!</i>

33
00:00:52,867 --> 00:00:54,700
<i>It'll be even harder
to find Golda now.</i>

34
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,367
<i> Because you showed yourself.</i>

35
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,733
<i>The woman who ruined my family
was right in front of me.</i>

36
00:00:58,867 --> 00:00:59,667
<i> Was I supposed to do nothing?</i>

37
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,067
<i> We all know that.</i>

38
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,267
<i> You're not using your brain.</i>

39
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,800
<i>Sorry, okay?
I'm not a robot like you.</i>

40
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:27,200
Fine, I'll have
the shipment prepared.

41
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:37,033
You seem happy.

42
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,267
I think my work here is done.

43
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:47,367
The smear campaign
against Delgado and Parak

44
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,333
is solidly in place.

45
00:01:49,467 --> 00:01:52,167
Everyone hates them.

46
00:01:53,367 --> 00:01:55,333
Look at this.

47
00:01:55,467 --> 00:01:57,533
“Make them suffer.”

48
00:01:57,667 --> 00:02:00,900
“Torture them.”
“Feed them to the ants

49
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:04,367
and to the crocodiles
like them.”

50
00:02:05,833 --> 00:02:07,000
Post a comment.

51
00:02:07,133 --> 00:02:09,333
Say it's done.

52
00:02:09,467 --> 00:02:12,300
The news is spreading so fast,

53
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:15,333
and the damage keeps on growing.

54
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:18,667
I love social media
and its netizens.

55
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,667
But we still haven't fixed
one problem.

56
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:25,067
Golda is also too slippery.

57
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:30,233
It's supposed
to be Parak's problem.

58
00:02:30,367 --> 00:02:33,067
That cop was reckless.

59
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:36,833
He's already dead but he left us
a problem to deal with.

60
00:02:45,633 --> 00:02:47,300
Loloy.

61
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:50,167
Any information about Golda?

62
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:51,667
None yet, Boss.

63
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:54,867
I asked all our dealers
like her.

64
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,067
No one knows where she is.

65
00:02:58,167 --> 00:03:00,567
Find her before she starts
to make a mess.

66
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:01,400
Now!

67
00:03:01,533 --> 00:03:02,900
Let's go.

68
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:25,133
Still thinking about Golda?

69
00:03:32,367 --> 00:03:35,267
I just don't know
what I'm doing wrong anymore.

70
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,333
I feel like everything's
falling apart.

71
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:47,867
The video...

72
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,200
Godfather Diego...

73
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:50,967
and now, Golda.

74
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,600
She was the only one
who could help me,

75
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:54,000
and now she's gone too.

76
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:56,867
I just want to help dad.

77
00:03:58,467 --> 00:04:02,300
But whatever I do,
I always messed it up.

78
00:04:05,467 --> 00:04:07,867
You know,
maybe Andrew is right.

79
00:04:08,767 --> 00:04:11,367
I'm the reason why everything
is falling apart.

80
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:13,400
No.

81
00:04:13,533 --> 00:04:14,667
No.

82
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:16,567
You're not.

83
00:04:32,667 --> 00:04:34,733
<i> Golda, you're guilty, right?</i>

84
00:04:34,867 --> 00:04:36,233
<i> Because I met Major Delgado.</i>

85
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:38,033
<i> He's a good man.</i>

86
00:04:38,167 --> 00:04:39,167
<i>That's why I know
you feel guilty</i>

87
00:04:39,300 --> 00:04:41,633
<i>about all the things
you did to him.</i>

88
00:04:55,033 --> 00:04:56,300
Elai, Kyle.

89
00:04:56,433 --> 00:04:58,300
Boss?

90
00:04:58,433 --> 00:04:59,667
Yes, Boss?

91
00:05:02,667 --> 00:05:04,033
Look for this.

92
00:05:04,167 --> 00:05:05,267
What is it?

93
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,367
It will lead us to Golda.

94
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:09,633
She's a valuable informant.

95
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,633
We have to find her.

96
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,233
Okay.

97
00:05:13,367 --> 00:05:14,900
- Yes, Boss.
- Let's go.

98
00:05:31,067 --> 00:05:32,567
You're going out?

99
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:34,567
We are going out.

100
00:05:34,733 --> 00:05:36,033
Get dressed.

101
00:05:36,167 --> 00:05:37,833
Where are we going?

102
00:05:37,967 --> 00:05:39,033
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

103
00:05:39,167 --> 00:05:40,267
I'm coming too.

104
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:42,067
Where to?

105
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,800
We can still track down, Golda.

106
00:05:43,933 --> 00:05:45,267
Let's go.

107
00:05:46,867 --> 00:05:48,433
How?

108
00:05:48,567 --> 00:05:51,300
I told you I don't know
where she is.

109
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:53,200
Dewi, please.

110
00:05:53,333 --> 00:05:56,300
We're sure you still have
contact with Golda.

111
00:05:56,433 --> 00:05:58,567
We just need
to talk to her, please.

112
00:05:58,700 --> 00:06:02,367
Sorry, I don't want to break
Golda's trust in me.

113
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:03,467
You, Oppa.

114
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:06,367
You used me.

115
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:08,200
You made me a fool.

116
00:06:12,433 --> 00:06:14,100
I'm sorry.

117
00:06:14,233 --> 00:06:16,533
Look, we just need to talk
to Golda.

118
00:06:18,633 --> 00:06:20,200
So...

119
00:06:20,333 --> 00:06:22,267
please tell me.

120
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:24,633
What can I do
to make it up to you?

121
00:06:24,767 --> 00:06:26,433
Don't do that.

122
00:06:26,567 --> 00:06:28,500
I'm weak when it comes to that.

123
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:49,900
Hello, Peter?

124
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:51,067
<i> Joey...</i>

125
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,433
The syndicate is here,
they're about to enter the spa.

126
00:06:53,567 --> 00:06:54,933
What?

127
00:07:00,167 --> 00:07:01,300
Go, go!

128
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,533
Excuse me.

129
00:07:07,667 --> 00:07:08,867
Where's Golda?

130
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,667
She's not here!

131
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,000
You won't tell us?

132
00:07:12,133 --> 00:07:13,067
Where is she?

133
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,700
Say it now!

134
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,067
They went in there.

135
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:48,433
They're coming.

136
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,200
Okay, okay.

137
00:07:59,800 --> 00:08:00,967
There they are.

138
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,600
Go! Go!

139
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:07,967
<i> Stop!</i>

140
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,000
<i> Jin Ho?</i>

141
00:08:10,333 --> 00:08:12,467
<i>What are you waiting for?
Shoot him!</i>

142
00:08:21,433 --> 00:08:22,567
- Call the police!
- I am!

143
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:24,433
Call the police!

144
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,167
We have to go!

145
00:08:35,567 --> 00:08:36,500
Hurry! Let's go!

146
00:08:36,633 --> 00:08:37,967
Wait!

147
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,333
Okay!

148
00:08:39,467 --> 00:08:40,467
Come on, hurry!

149
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,133
- You go, first!
- Come on, hurry!

150
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:54,333
Go! Go!

151
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,767
- It's locked!
- Yes, over the gate.

152
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:02,700
Just climb the gate.

153
00:09:06,033 --> 00:09:08,000
Hey, this way! This way!

154
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:23,700
We are going to die!
Who are they?

155
00:09:23,833 --> 00:09:25,100
Do not look! Hide!

156
00:09:25,233 --> 00:09:28,100
Don't scold us!
It's not our fault!

157
00:09:30,733 --> 00:09:32,900
We'll get out of here!
Just hide!

158
00:09:41,667 --> 00:09:43,133
Joey, where are you?

159
00:09:43,267 --> 00:09:45,100
There are so many gunshots,
are you okay?

160
00:09:45,233 --> 00:09:46,533
Peter...

161
00:09:46,667 --> 00:09:47,600
we went out the back.

162
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:49,400
Golda's cousin is with us.

163
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,300
I see a road here at the back.

164
00:09:52,433 --> 00:09:53,433
Go here.

165
00:09:53,567 --> 00:09:54,767
Okay, I'll circle around.

166
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,100
Okay, okay.

167
00:10:01,567 --> 00:10:03,400
Jin Ho, Peter is coming!

168
00:10:03,533 --> 00:10:04,600
Okay, go, Joey.

169
00:10:04,733 --> 00:10:06,233
Take care, I'll cover you.

170
00:10:06,367 --> 00:10:07,267
How about you?

171
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:08,567
Don't worry, I'm okay.

172
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:10,733
I'll meet you
at the boarding house, promise.

173
00:10:10,867 --> 00:10:11,767
Okay.

174
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,333
On the count of three,
you run, okay?

175
00:10:14,467 --> 00:10:15,967
Okay.

176
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:17,900
One...

177
00:10:18,033 --> 00:10:19,733
Two...

178
00:10:19,867 --> 00:10:21,233
Three! You run!

179
00:10:30,067 --> 00:10:32,400
Joey, let's go!

180
00:10:32,533 --> 00:10:33,367
Wait.

181
00:10:41,767 --> 00:10:43,267
Jin Ho!

182
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:47,167
Go!

183
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:49,533
Joey, come on, let's go!
Let's move ahead!

184
00:10:49,667 --> 00:10:51,333
Get out of here!

185
00:10:51,467 --> 00:10:52,867
- Joey, we have to go first!
- Joey!

186
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,633
Let's leave them!

187
00:11:10,733 --> 00:11:12,400
I'll verify that part, okay?

188
00:11:12,533 --> 00:11:13,767
Just wait.

189
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,667
Boss...

190
00:11:23,533 --> 00:11:24,933
I got something.

191
00:11:25,067 --> 00:11:26,567
What is it?

192
00:11:26,700 --> 00:11:28,133
<i> Batikang Ganda?</i>

193
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:29,267
Yup.

194
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,467
It's a women's clothing
and lifestyle store.

195
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:33,033
They only have one branch.

196
00:11:33,167 --> 00:11:34,833
Their products are handmade,

197
00:11:34,967 --> 00:11:37,933
and their fabrics are sourced
from abroad.

198
00:11:38,867 --> 00:11:40,233
Where's the store located?

199
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:41,933
Wait, I'll check.

200
00:11:47,567 --> 00:11:48,767
Where are they now?

201
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:50,333
Looks like they managed
to escape, Boss.

202
00:11:50,467 --> 00:11:52,300
It's impossible for them
to get that far that fast.

203
00:11:53,633 --> 00:11:55,167
Let's move.

204
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,667
Let's go, Bro!

205
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:17,467
Here.

206
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,400
Pass me a glass, Joey.

207
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:23,800
You know, I already checked.

208
00:12:23,933 --> 00:12:25,600
No one's following us,
we're safe.

209
00:12:25,733 --> 00:12:29,433
Good thing Jin Ho blocked
the ones chasing you.

210
00:12:29,567 --> 00:12:31,067
It was effective.

211
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:33,367
Good thing that Korean is brave

212
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,333
even if he's a bit
of a trickster.

213
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:39,367
It's really good you came
with us, Dewi.

214
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,633
At least, you weren't caught
by the ones chasing us earlier.

215
00:12:41,767 --> 00:12:43,233
Exactly,
that's what I was thinking.

216
00:12:43,367 --> 00:12:46,767
If not, I'd probably be dead.

217
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,933
Thank you, really.

218
00:12:50,967 --> 00:12:51,700
I wonder where Jin Ho is.

219
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:54,433
He's still not answering.

220
00:12:54,567 --> 00:12:56,567
Joey, you'll just put him
in more danger

221
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:58,333
if you keep calling.

222
00:12:58,467 --> 00:12:59,333
That's enough.

223
00:12:59,467 --> 00:13:01,833
I'm worried, he got shot.

224
00:13:03,133 --> 00:13:05,867
Come on, that's probably just
like an ant bite to him.

225
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,333
Isn't he Korean intelligence?

226
00:13:08,467 --> 00:13:10,833
That means he's used to combat.

227
00:13:10,967 --> 00:13:13,100
- Don't worry.
- But, still...

228
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:16,233
And you know what?
He stayed behind

229
00:13:16,367 --> 00:13:18,400
just to make sure Dewi and I
got away safely.

230
00:13:30,533 --> 00:13:32,933
He's still not answering,
where could he be?

231
00:13:34,767 --> 00:13:36,267
- Jin Ho!
- Oppa!

232
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:38,000
We were worried about you!

233
00:13:39,167 --> 00:13:40,067
I'm okay.

234
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,500
You're bleeding.

235
00:13:42,933 --> 00:13:44,233
It's nothing.

236
00:13:44,367 --> 00:13:46,667
There is more important
things to do.

237
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,000
No, let's go to the hospital.

238
00:13:48,133 --> 00:13:49,100
- You have to get checked.
- No, no, no.

239
00:13:49,233 --> 00:13:50,433
I'm really okay.

240
00:13:50,567 --> 00:13:51,967
No worries.

241
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,233
So...

242
00:13:57,367 --> 00:13:59,200
are you ready to tell us...

243
00:13:59,333 --> 00:14:00,467
where Golda is?

244
00:14:13,567 --> 00:14:15,667
Dewi's asleep,
she got exhausted.

245
00:14:17,067 --> 00:14:19,400
Oh, what's that?

246
00:14:19,533 --> 00:14:20,567
What's that?

247
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:22,500
A tetanus shot.

248
00:14:23,667 --> 00:14:26,000
I always bring one,
just in case,

249
00:14:26,133 --> 00:14:28,367
for situation like this.

250
00:14:28,533 --> 00:14:30,200
You know, here in our country...

251
00:14:31,167 --> 00:14:33,100
we just use soap for tetanus.

252
00:14:33,233 --> 00:14:34,833
Laundry bar soap.

253
00:14:34,967 --> 00:14:38,067
A shot? That's over the top.

254
00:14:40,233 --> 00:14:42,133
Let me help you.

255
00:14:42,267 --> 00:14:43,867
I'll do it.

256
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:44,933
Let me do it.

257
00:14:45,067 --> 00:14:46,367
What?

258
00:14:47,333 --> 00:14:48,733
Let me see.

259
00:14:50,367 --> 00:14:52,033
It's not even that deep.

260
00:14:52,167 --> 00:14:54,033
You have nothing
to worry about.

261
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,433
Why? Does it hurt?

262
00:14:59,567 --> 00:15:00,433
- It hurts, right?
- Hey.

263
00:15:00,567 --> 00:15:02,433
It's not even that deep, see?

264
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:04,100
Get off of me, man.

265
00:15:06,167 --> 00:15:07,600
You know what,
let's just talk about Golda.

266
00:15:07,733 --> 00:15:09,233
Joey!

267
00:15:10,500 --> 00:15:12,367
What are you doing here?

268
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:13,433
Oh, what?

269
00:15:13,567 --> 00:15:15,533
Do you have a wound too?

270
00:15:15,667 --> 00:15:17,167
Wait, what happened there?

271
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,867
Long story.

272
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,467
- We went...
- Later, later.

273
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:23,333
I have something
more important to say.

274
00:15:24,233 --> 00:15:26,700
I know where we can find Golda.

275
00:15:27,633 --> 00:15:28,967
We already know too.

276
00:15:30,267 --> 00:15:31,767
- In Amoroso.
- In Amoroso.

277
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:35,100
How did you find out?

278
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:40,367
From the logo on Golda's shirt
when we went to see her.

279
00:15:40,500 --> 00:15:42,500
There's only one store
with that logo, Joey.

280
00:15:42,633 --> 00:15:44,333
It's in Amoroso.

281
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:46,533
What about you?

282
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,967
How did you find out?

283
00:15:50,167 --> 00:15:52,400
From Dewi, Golda's cousin.

284
00:15:52,533 --> 00:15:54,067
She finally admitted it.

285
00:15:56,533 --> 00:15:58,133
Well, I guess, it's nice.

286
00:15:58,267 --> 00:16:01,400
All I knew was the store,

287
00:16:01,533 --> 00:16:03,667
but I didn't know the exact
location.

288
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:07,733
At least, her cousin told you
where Golda really is.

289
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:10,300
Not exactly where.

290
00:16:10,433 --> 00:16:13,233
Of course, Golda's scared
of being followed.

291
00:16:13,867 --> 00:16:18,000
What's important is we know
she goes home to Amoroso.

292
00:16:18,133 --> 00:16:19,733
I guess...

293
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:22,233
we're going to Amoroso.

294
00:16:25,533 --> 00:16:27,733
We got nothing
from the spa, Boss.

295
00:16:27,867 --> 00:16:30,033
The therapists didn't know
anything.

296
00:16:30,167 --> 00:16:32,033
The manager,
who's Golda's cousin,

297
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:34,567
we almost caught her.

298
00:16:34,700 --> 00:16:35,700
Almost?

299
00:16:35,833 --> 00:16:36,967
She got away, Ma'am.

300
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,000
The Korean helped her

301
00:16:39,133 --> 00:16:41,433
the one we had
a run-in with before.

302
00:16:43,433 --> 00:16:45,900
What does he have to do
with Golda?

303
00:16:46,033 --> 00:16:47,900
Not Golda, you.

304
00:16:48,833 --> 00:16:52,100
He definitely has an idea
about our organization.

305
00:16:52,233 --> 00:16:54,367
He's watching our every move.

306
00:16:55,333 --> 00:16:58,233
He'll use anyone...

307
00:16:58,367 --> 00:17:00,067
just to get closer to you.

308
00:17:01,267 --> 00:17:04,700
Looks like he wants to sabotage
everything we're doing.

309
00:17:04,833 --> 00:17:06,200
Exactly.

310
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:09,233
You won't even realize it...

311
00:17:09,367 --> 00:17:11,300
you're already walking
straight towards him.

312
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:17,433
That bastard.

313
00:17:17,567 --> 00:17:19,800
He really won't stop.

314
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:21,433
Fine.

315
00:17:21,567 --> 00:17:23,133
I'll turn the heat up

316
00:17:23,267 --> 00:17:26,300
and burn his whole game down.

317
00:17:37,267 --> 00:17:38,367
Wait, wait, wait.

318
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,033
What? All of us are going?

319
00:17:40,167 --> 00:17:41,533
Even you, Joey?

320
00:17:41,667 --> 00:17:43,067
Even him?

321
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,767
Are you sure you trust him?

322
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,133
And why wouldn't she?

323
00:17:46,267 --> 00:17:48,767
I'm part of finding Golda.

324
00:17:48,933 --> 00:17:51,633
Wait, who said the two of you
are coming?

325
00:17:51,767 --> 00:17:53,200
I don't trust you.

326
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:55,100
I only trust Joey.

327
00:17:56,567 --> 00:17:58,533
So when I said “we,”

328
00:17:58,667 --> 00:18:02,500
I meant just the two of us.

329
00:18:02,633 --> 00:18:03,800
You're not invited.

330
00:18:03,933 --> 00:18:05,133
You're pretty bossy.

331
00:18:05,267 --> 00:18:07,900
Joey's the only one
who gets to decide, not you.

332
00:18:12,267 --> 00:18:14,300
I'm Joey's bodyguard,

333
00:18:14,433 --> 00:18:17,700
and she's not going anywhere
without me.

334
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:18,933
Same!

335
00:18:19,067 --> 00:18:20,733
I'm her plus-one.

336
00:18:20,867 --> 00:18:22,333
I'm her best friend.

337
00:18:24,133 --> 00:18:26,267
You know,
if I'm going to Amoroso,

338
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,267
of course, I'd ask for help...

339
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:30,433
and the three of you are exactly
who I'd think to bring.

340
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:32,000
See? There you go.

341
00:18:32,133 --> 00:18:34,067
But if you're all going
to keep fighting,

342
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,367
then I'll just go alone.

343
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,933
We might mess this up
if you keep acting like that.

344
00:18:41,433 --> 00:18:43,633
So what?
Are you still going to argue?

345
00:18:43,767 --> 00:18:46,567
If it's just to find Golda,
fine.

346
00:18:50,667 --> 00:18:52,033
Peter?

347
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:57,500
Okay, fine, Peter.

348
00:18:58,767 --> 00:18:59,867
All right.

349
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,133
Jin Ho.

350
00:19:02,500 --> 00:19:03,933
Fine.

351
00:19:04,067 --> 00:19:07,000
Okay, good.
So we're all going, okay?

352
00:19:29,867 --> 00:19:31,667
Where are you going?
I'll sit there, I'll sit there.

353
00:19:31,933 --> 00:19:32,600
I'll sit here.

354
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,667
Wait, are we really going
to fight over the seat too?

355
00:19:35,933 --> 00:19:37,367
Yes, even the seat.

356
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:38,733
Why?

357
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,800
Fine, sit there.

358
00:19:41,933 --> 00:19:44,133
Joey and I will sit at the back.

359
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:45,767
Wait, wait, wait.

360
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:48,500
I'll just sit at the back.

361
00:19:48,633 --> 00:19:50,267
It's spacious.

362
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,933
Smells nice, I'll stay here.

363
00:19:52,067 --> 00:19:53,433
Stay there.

364
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,767
Okay?

365
00:20:02,233 --> 00:20:03,200
Andrew...

366
00:20:07,167 --> 00:20:08,000
Yes?

367
00:20:09,033 --> 00:20:10,633
I just wanted to thank you

368
00:20:10,767 --> 00:20:14,867
for coming to tell me
where Golda was.

369
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
But you didn't need it.

370
00:20:17,867 --> 00:20:19,033
Right?

371
00:20:19,167 --> 00:20:21,033
Actually, you know what?
You're really good.

372
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:22,633
I admire you.

373
00:20:22,767 --> 00:20:25,000
You managed to do that
on your own.

374
00:20:25,133 --> 00:20:27,400
You found Golda.

375
00:20:30,433 --> 00:20:33,367
Not really, Jin Ho and Peter
were with me.

376
00:20:34,133 --> 00:20:35,700
But...

377
00:20:35,867 --> 00:20:38,933
I really appreciate that...

378
00:20:39,067 --> 00:20:41,067
even after the not-so-nice
things I said to you,

379
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,133
you still wanted to help me.

380
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,633
So thank you, Andrew.

381
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:51,233
What are you doing back there?
Let's go!

382
00:20:57,767 --> 00:20:59,467
Come on. Let's go.

383
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,433
I don't want to get complacent,

384
00:21:21,567 --> 00:21:23,400
especially since others are also
looking for Golda.

385
00:21:23,533 --> 00:21:25,433
- Golda.
- Godfather!

386
00:21:25,567 --> 00:21:27,667
When was the last time
you spoke to Braganza?

387
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:30,767
Our clients are with him now.

388
00:21:30,900 --> 00:21:32,167
Miss, may I ask something?

389
00:21:32,300 --> 00:21:34,200
Do you know someone named
Golda Briones?

390
00:21:34,333 --> 00:21:35,533
I think that's Golda.

391
00:21:35,667 --> 00:21:36,433
Golda!

392
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:38,467
That's Golda's car.

393
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:39,633
Let's just follow it.

394
00:21:39,767 --> 00:21:42,100
I'm sure it'll lead us to her.

395
00:21:42,267 --> 00:21:43,700
My friend replied already

396
00:21:43,833 --> 00:21:46,033
about the plate number
you asked us to check.

397
00:21:46,167 --> 00:21:47,567
It's registered
to Vincente Alcala.

398
00:21:47,700 --> 00:21:51,500
Do you know the one
they call Godfather?

399
00:21:51,633 --> 00:21:52,533
Godfather?

400
00:21:52,667 --> 00:21:54,067
She went into hiding
under another syndicate.

401
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:56,367
Braganza has a target
here in Luzon.

402
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:58,200
There's going to be a party
at Godfather's place.

403
00:21:58,333 --> 00:21:59,833
Guess who got an invite.

404
00:21:59,967 --> 00:22:01,533
Then we have no other choice

405
00:22:01,667 --> 00:22:04,233
but to infiltrate
that Godfather's villa.
